### RoleCall Backend — End-to-End Smoke Test
### Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension or IntelliJ's built-in HTTP client.
### Run `docker compose up --build` first and wait for all services to report healthy
### (`docker compose ps`). All requests go through the gateway on :8080.

@gateway = http://localhost:8080

### 0a. Health checks
GET {{gateway}}/actuator/health

### 0b.
GET http://localhost:8761
# Eureka dashboard — confirm all 7 services (gateway + 5 business + itself) are registered

### 1. Register an employer
# @name registerEmployer
POST {{gateway}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "employer@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "role": "EMPLOYER"
}

### 2. Register a candidate
# @name registerCandidate
POST {{gateway}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "candidate@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

###
@employerToken = {{registerEmployer.response.body.accessToken}}
@employerId = {{registerEmployer.response.body.userId}}
@candidateToken = {{registerCandidate.response.body.accessToken}}
@candidateId = {{registerCandidate.response.body.userId}}

### 3. Confirm user-service asynchronously created both profile shells
# (May need a retry if run immediately — Kafka consumption is async.)
GET {{gateway}}/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{employerToken}}

###
GET {{gateway}}/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{candidateToken}}

### 4. Employer posts a job
# @name createJob
POST {{gateway}}/api/jobs
Authorization: Bearer {{employerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Backend Engineer",
  "description": "Build and operate our Spring Boot services.",
  "company": "Acme Inc",
  "location": "Remote",
  "type": "FULL_TIME",
  "arrangement": "REMOTE",
  "experienceLevel": "2-4 years",
  "salaryMin": 90000,
  "salaryMax": 130000
}

###
@jobId = {{createJob.response.body.id}}

### 5. Browse jobs — public, no token, paginated to match the frontend's 9-per-page grid
GET {{gateway}}/api/jobs?search=Backend&page=0&size=9

### 6. Candidate applies
# @name apply
POST {{gateway}}/api/applications
Authorization: Bearer {{candidateToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "jobId": "{{jobId}}"
}

###
@applicationId = {{apply.response.body.id}}

### 7. Confirm applicantCount incremented (async via Kafka — retry if it shows 0 immediately)
GET {{gateway}}/api/jobs/{{jobId}}

### 8. Employer views applicants for the job
GET {{gateway}}/api/applications/job/{{jobId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{employerToken}}

### 9. Employer moves the application to UNDER_REVIEW
PUT {{gateway}}/api/applications/{{applicationId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{employerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "UNDER_REVIEW",
  "note": "Looks promising"
}

### 10. Employer starts a Stripe Checkout Session to feature the job
# @name checkout
POST {{gateway}}/api/payments/checkout-session
Authorization: Bearer {{employerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "jobId": "{{jobId}}"
}

### Open checkout.checkoutUrl in a browser and pay with Stripe's test card 4242 4242 4242 4242.
### Stripe can't reach localhost directly — run the Stripe CLI alongside docker compose:
###   stripe listen --forward-to localhost:8080/api/payments/webhook
### After a successful payment, confirm the job flipped to FEATURED:
GET {{gateway}}/api/jobs/{{jobId}}

### --- Negative cases ---

### 11. Expired/garbage token -> 401 at the gateway
GET {{gateway}}/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer not-a-real-token

### 12. Candidate attempting to post a job -> 403
POST {{gateway}}/api/jobs
Authorization: Bearer {{candidateToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Should be rejected",
  "description": "N/A",
  "company": "N/A",
  "location": "N/A",
  "type": "FULL_TIME",
  "arrangement": "REMOTE",
  "experienceLevel": "0-2 years"
}

### 13. Candidate applying twice to the same job -> 409
POST {{gateway}}/api/applications
Authorization: Bearer {{candidateToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "jobId": "{{jobId}}"
}
